From: MacRunner <noreply@macrunner.app>
Subject: [PATCH] winemac.drv: arm64 fallback for CAMetalLayer when D3DMetal unavailable

CrossOver's d3dmetal_objc.h declares WineMetalLayer only under
__x86_64__ (since D3DMetal is x86_64-only by Apple's licensing).
But cocoa_window.m used WineMetalLayer unconditionally, which breaks
the arm64-native winemac.drv build.

This patch adds a plain CAMetalLayer fallback for non-x86_64 hosts.
On arm64 native, D3DMetal is not in the path anyway — graphics go
through DXMT or DXVK+MoltenVK.

---
 dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
@@ -982,7 +982,12 @@

     - (CALayer*) makeBackingLayer
     {
+#if defined(__x86_64__)
         CAMetalLayer *layer = [WineMetalLayer layer];   /* CW HACK 22435 — D3DMetal only on x86_64 */
+#else
+        /* MacRunner: on arm64 native host, D3DMetal is not used; plain CAMetalLayer is fine. */
+        CAMetalLayer *layer = [CAMetalLayer layer];
+#endif
         layer.device = _device;
         layer.framebufferOnly = YES;
         layer.magnificationFilter = kCAFilterNearest;
